  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Description\n\nI am submitting a bug report regarding an issue where VRChat fails to clear its content cache despite extensive troubleshooting. Even after closing the application and manually deleting the entire Cache folder located in %LocalAppData%Low\\VRChat\\VRChat, the in-game storage metrics and cached asset files persist or immediately re-index upon relaunch as if no deletion occurred. I have verified folder permissions to rule out read-only restrictions, tested launcher file integrity, and reinstalled the application entirely, yet the cache remains uncleared. I have attached my latest output logs detailing this failure for further diagnostic review.\n\nReproduction Steps\n\nHow to make this bug happen: No special steps are required. Simply launch VRChat, log in as usual, and navigate to the Debug/Storage settings. The content cache fails to clear automatically or display as empty, even after the cache folder has been manually deleted on the system prior to launching the application.\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: Other\n\n- Frequency: Always\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.3.2p1-1902-20253ca7ae-Release\n\nunityVersion: 2022.3.22f2-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report",
